From: fix session 2026-09-12
Subject: [PATCH 0038] wasm64 speculation: narrow successor addresses to the guest address width

`w64_speculate()` (0019/0020) turns recorded successor addresses into
real `tb_gen_code()` calls, so unlike upstream — which only same-page
tests them — it needs them to be architecturally valid addresses.  Two
sources handed it 64-bit values that a 32-bit guest can never produce:

  - `translator_note_succ()` takes whatever the frontend computed, and
    `gen_goto_tb()` builds a branch target as a 64-bit `s->pc_curr +
    diff`.  A target that wraps around zero on a 32-bit guest therefore
    arrives sign-extended.
  - the `ldr pc, [pc, #-4]` trampoline literal is read with
    `ldl_le_p()`, which returns a *signed* int: any literal with bit 31
    set (0xa0000000 flash/RAM, 0xffff0000 high vectors) sign-extends.

A sign-extended address that still passes the non-faulting probe reaches
`tb_gen_code()`, and `translator_ld()` then compares a sign-extended
`db->pc_first` against a pc the frontend zero-extended: neither page
test matches and it aborts on `(base ^ pc) & TARGET_PAGE_MASK`.

KE800 died there ~90 s into the boot on dist-jit: a one-insn TB at guest
0x0 branches back by -0xebb0, wrapping into the 0xffff0000 high vectors
where its firmware runs the GSM L1 interrupt path (S75/EL71 reach the
same trampolines, but never with a wrapping branch, so only the LG board
tripped it).

Narrow in both places.  The truncated value is the architectural target
— a 32-bit branch wraps in hardware exactly this way — so no successor
is lost, and `TCG_TYPE_I32` keeps 64-bit guests untouched.

Verified: KE800 boots to its idle screen on dist-jit (previously an
abort or a wedged vCPU); S75/EL71 unchanged; wasm64 lockstep clean.

--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -714,7 +714,20 @@
             if (w64_spec_code_host(env, last, mmu_idx, &h1) &&
                 ldl_le_p(h1) == 0xe51ff004 &&
                 w64_spec_code_host(env, last + 4, mmu_idx, &h2)) {
-                vaddr target = ldl_le_p(h2);
+                /*
+                 * ldl_le_p() returns a *signed* int: a literal with bit
+                 * 31 set (0xa0000000 flash/RAM, and the 0xffff0000 high
+                 * vectors the pmb887x bootrom lives in) sign-extends into
+                 * the 64-bit vaddr.  A sign-extended address that still
+                 * passes the probe reaches tb_gen_code, and translator_ld
+                 * then compares db->pc_first (sign-extended) against a pc
+                 * the ARM frontend zero-extended: neither page test
+                 * matches and it aborts on
+                 * "(base ^ pc) & TARGET_PAGE_MASK".  KE800 died there
+                 * ~90 s into the boot (its firmware runs the GSM L1
+                 * interrupt path through the 0xffff0000 trampolines).
+                 */
+                vaddr target = (uint32_t)ldl_le_p(h2);
                 if (!(target & 3)) {
                     succ[nsucc++] = target;
                 }

--- a/accel/tcg/translator.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translator.c
@@ -114,6 +114,23 @@
     TranslationBlock *tb = db->tb;
     unsigned i;
 
+    /*
+     * Narrow to the guest's address width.  The frontends compute a
+     * branch target as a 64-bit `pc + diff` (gen_goto_tb) and hand it
+     * over unnarrowed: on a 32-bit guest a target that wraps around zero
+     * arrives sign-extended.  Upstream only same-page-tests the value, so
+     * a wrong high half merely disables goto_tb, but w64_speculate feeds
+     * it to tb_gen_code as a real address — and translator_ld then aborts
+     * on "(base ^ pc) & TARGET_PAGE_MASK", comparing a sign-extended
+     * db->pc_first against a pc the frontend zero-extended.  KE800 died
+     * there ~90 s in: a TB at guest 0x0 branches back by -0xebb0 into the
+     * 0xffff0000 high vectors, which is where its GSM L1 interrupt path
+     * lives.
+     */
+    if (tcg_ctx->addr_type == TCG_TYPE_I32) {
+        dest = (uint32_t)dest;
+    }
+
     for (i = 0; i < tb->w64_nsucc; i++) {
         if (tb->w64_succ[i] == dest) {
             return;
